        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Elbow cushion of woven silk (kesi), China, 1700-1750"@en , "Hexagonal elbow cushion of dark blue woven silk (kesi) with coloured silks and golden gilt thread.\n\nEach of the six side panels has a similar design of a five clawed dragon in profile, with clouds, waves and mountains. The two circular panels, in the top and bottom, each have designs of a facing dragon, with clouds, waves and mountains."@en ;
